@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] boot-log-no-elevation-or-payload-diagnostics
The logger MUST run without setuid bits or file capabilities, invoke the command
directly without a shell, and persist only the bounded boot log file. Child
payload bytes reach the private log file only; they never become messages on
the helper's own stdout, stderr or any diagnostic stream.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] boot-log-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover selector refusal, the `open_log` custody matrix
(absent, regular, hard-linked, symlinked and directory paths across modes and
readers, run as the current uid), exact bounded retention and drain across
generated sizes, chunking-independent line timestamps and the `push_prefix`
format against independent oracles, and `settle` exit-code preservation and
signal re-raise against short-lived fixture children. Nonblocking discard
under flood, the helper's own signal death and the reader handover keep
process-level fixtures (a handover to a foreign uid runs only as root); no
root or KVM is required.
